{
  "date": "2026-09-30",
  "period_start": "2026-09-01",
  "period_end": "2026-09-30",
  "title": "One API, more kinds of work",
  "summary": "September made more models and media usable through familiar APIs, while giving agents, community apps, and builders better places to work and be found.\n\nThe model shelf grew across text, image, video, and speech. Chat and Responses gained native media routes, and a new Anthropic-compatible Messages endpoint opened another path for existing clients.\n\nManaged agents gained structured, replayable results, GitHub-backed deployment, a persistent Computer MCP workspace, and client-defined tools. Polli and MCP integrations made those capabilities easier to use from coding tools.\n\nNew apps, agents, plugins, and routers covered comics, developer tools, image editing, Arabic-language interfaces, and more. App Quests connected approved submissions to claimable Pollen rewards.\n\nModel listings gained clearer capabilities, health, and route information; Enter and account activity became easier to navigate. Website v2 closed the month with a new home page and a searchable, shareable Apps directory.",
  "pr_count": 506,
